{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And from</b> — the sense is: from one of these kingdoms came forth a little horn in the size of its army, namely that which was in the land of Israel, in Antioch, and he is Antiochus. It grew great over the kingdom of Egypt, south of the land of Israel, for the latitude of Egypt from the equator is twenty-nine degrees and the latitude of Jerusalem is thirty-three, therefore it is in the middle of the inhabited world, for all of it extends to sixty-six degrees from the equator, for twenty-four degrees is the inclination of the zodiacal sphere from the plane of the equator. And the sense of east is the land of Persia." "<b>Toward the glorious</b> — the entire land of Israel is the glory of all lands."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The geographical-astronomical argument is preserved as written; 'degrees' renders מעלות (arc-degrees of latitude), and 'equator' renders הקו השוה."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:20:25.826304675Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}